ubuntu-hello (1.2.0-1ppa1) resolute; urgency=high

  * Security hardening of the root PAM compare helper's process environment
    and child lookups (reported by an automated vulnerability scanner as a
    potential local privilege escalation via a user-controlled PATH; on
    review it was NOT exploitable as described -- see below -- but the code
    relied on unspecified libc behaviour, so it is now explicit).
  * pam_ubuntu_hello.so now spawns compare.py with posix_spawn() and an
    explicit minimal environment (only PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin)
    instead of a NULL envp, and starts the interpreter with
    "python3 -E -s" (ignore PYTHON* variables, no user site-packages). The
    calling user's PATH, PYTHONPATH, LD_PRELOAD, etc. can never reach the
    root helper. -I was deliberately not used: it would also drop the
    script directory from sys.path, breaking compare.py's sibling imports.
  * compare.py now starts the auth overlay via an absolute path
    (GTK_BIN_PATH = /usr/bin/ubuntu-hello-gtk), matching the existing
    BUSCTL_PATH pattern, instead of a bare "ubuntu-hello-gtk" PATH lookup.
  * Why it was not exploitable before: on glibc/Linux, posix_spawnp() with
    a NULL envp gives the child an EMPTY environment (verified with a test
    program), not the caller's; with no PATH set, both execvp() and
    Python's subprocess fall back to /bin:/usr/bin, so ~/.local/bin was
    never searched. The fix removes the dependency on that corner case.
  * Docs: docs/SECURITY.md gains a "No Inherited Environment / PATH"
    bullet; docs/architecture/README.md and AGENTS.md updated to describe
    the explicit-env spawn and -E -s flags.
  * Tests: new regression test test_auth_overlay_uses_absolute_gtk_path in
    tests/test_compare_cleanup.py; PAM module builds clean and meson C++
    tests pass.
  * Fix: TPM-sealed keyring unlock failed under polkit (worked at GDM):
    polkit >= 126 runs polkit-agent-helper-1 with DevicePolicy=strict and
    ProtectSystem=strict; the drop-in now also allows char-tpm, /dev/tpm0
    and ReadWritePaths=/etc/ubuntu-hello/tpm-keys (install.sh,
    package-configure.sh, install_config.py). Verified live. The same
    drop-in sets ProtectHome=tmpfs + BindPaths=/run/user (yes hid
    /run/user, the session bus, so desktop notifications never reached the
    user from polkit prompts; /home and /root stay empty in the unit) and
    ReadWritePaths=-/run/ubuntu-hello; a new tmpfiles.d
    entry creates /run/ubuntu-hello{,/notify} at boot.
  * Setup wizard: second face model under different lighting (two-pass
    slide 4 with why/how instructions; skip either pass but not both;
    non-fatal second-scan failure; labels "Setup lighting 1/2"). The
    Settings Models tab shows a reminder with an "Add a second model"
    action while exactly one model is enrolled.
  * New: native desktop notification per face-auth attempt (notify.py):
    one card updated in place -- "Looking for your face..." stays up for
    the whole scan (critical urgency), then "Face recognized . sudo --
    Full Name . 1.3 s" (removed after success_linger = 3 s) or "No match
    in 8 s . add a model in this light" (stays in the list). Titles name
    the PAM service (forwarded as compare.py argv[2]). Notification id
    persisted per user so attempts reuse the same card; detached helper
    closes the success card / watchdogs a dead helper. [notifications]
    enabled/details/success_linger. Sent on the target user's session
    bus after dropping root; best-effort. New dep libglib2.0-bin.
  * Settings: Notifications tab (show notifications / sounds / diagnostics)
    backed by a comment-preserving config editor; "Add new user" removed.
    Setup wizard: Back navigation with per-page cleanup (scan cancelled,
    single camera list, chosen camera kept, second scan resumed); first
    scan required, second skippable. New Yaru-style app icon (SVG +
    symbolic, hicolor) and regenerated banner.
  * GTK 4 migration: Settings app, setup wizard and auth overlay now use
    GTK 4 + GtkBuilder .ui (main.ui, onboarding.ui; Glade files removed).
    Fixes the Language combo popup filling the whole screen on GTK 3.
    Stock widgets kept; gtk4compat.py wraps the removed GTK 3 calls
    (Gtk.main, Dialog.run, get_children, connect_signals). Camera
    previews and logos use GtkPicture; the wizard and Settings apply the
    user's GTK theme name (Yaru accent, light/dark) when elevated; wrapping
    labels are capped so windows stop growing. No GTK 4.10-deprecated
    widgets remain (DropDown, ColumnView, AlertDialog, Revealer banner);
    every wizard page and Settings tab shares one page idiom (glyph,
    title, hint, cards); tab switches no longer pop dropdown lists open.
    Language switch: content rebuilt inside the same toplevel (recreating
    the window crashed mutter 50 -> session logout), deferred rebuild
    after the list closes (no more freeze), .ui strings
    translated via Python gettext, dynamic _() in all modules; RTL
    languages (ar/he/fa/ur/ps/sd/yi) mirror the UI, with an E2E audit.
    About page links to GitHub issues (opened in the user's browser with
    the session env). Language-switch freeze root cause (Wayland grabbing
    popup mapped by the search reveal walker) fixed; dropdown and
    settings search match substrings, ignore case/accents; Escape clears,
    Ctrl+F focuses search. Cameras named by brand/model from udev; dropdown
    popups show full names; app icon recentred. Unit + E2E regressions for
    every manual find.
    Runtime
    dependency gir1.2-gtk-3.0 -> gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (RPM/Arch: gtk3 -> gtk4);
    all UH_CI_DE compat cells build and run the real-GTK E2E on GTK 4.
  * Review fixes: root notification state kept in root-owned
    /run/ubuntu-hello/notify (O_NOFOLLOW, no chown) instead of the
    user-writable /run/user/<uid>; privilege drop via subprocess
    user=/group= instead of preexec_fn; late progress card cannot
    overwrite a result; watchdog killed on result; success card only after
    rubberstamp liveness (exit 15 -> "Liveness check failed"); no_model
    card reachable; PAM forwards validated LANG/LC_* and compare.py
    applies the target user's language preference.
  * Dependency updates (product + CI) to latest final releases: dlib
    19.24.x -> 20.0.1 (postinst pip build and snap payload; verified to
    build from source on Ubuntu 26.04 / Python 3.14), inih Meson wrap
    r53 -> r62, Flatpak runtime/SDK 25.08 -> 26.08, Dockerfile frontend
    1.26.0 -> 1.27.0, CI coverage 7.15.4 -> 7.16.1, archlinux base-devel
    snapshot 20260816 -> 20260906, docker/setup-qemu-action v4.3.0,
    softprops/action-gh-release v3.0.3. fedora:44 kept (45 not yet final);
    snap base core24 kept (core26 migration is a separate follow-up).

